                <pb facs="0296" n="284" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg284"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">875.01/11–144: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Mr. Alexander C. Kirk,
                        Political Adviser, Allied Force Headquarters at Caserta</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-06T16:00:00-04:00">November 6, 1944—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>346. The Department hopes that you will continue to keep it informed regarding
                    developments in Albania. We should like particularly to have any details that
                    may come to your attention regarding the circumstances surrounding the
                    resignation of the Tirana Government and the extent to which FNC has established
                    its authority over the country.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
